{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291864-regular-spheres-vs-technocratic-spheres","id":1291864,"title":"Regular Spheres vs Technocratic Spheres","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-25T09:45:59-08:00","id":1291864,"title":"Regular Spheres vs Technocratic Spheres","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I would like the forum help to understand the Technocratic Spheres compared with the regular Spheres <b>in M20</b>, I would like to see if my comparisons are accurate, or where I am mistaken:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Spirit vs Dimensional Science: <s>Essentially the same, no measurable difference.</s> Dimensional Science allows manipulation of the Gauntlet, raising or lowering it, using an inverse Gauntlet chart. No exorcisms, no <i>Gilgul</i>.</li> <li>Correspondence vs Data: Ups and downs, Data gives you a nearly permanent connection to its targets and its better at information processing, but it wont work with say, those that don't use internet/cellphones (any Luddite group) nor extra planetary creatures/locations.</li> <li>Prime vs Primal Utility: Primal Utility is Prime+, you can do everything that regular old Prime <i>PLUS </i>ventures to generate Quintessence. Is there any downside to this?</li> </ol>Thanks for your time,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-18-2019, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T10:09:05-08:00","id":1291868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291864-regular-spheres-vs-technocratic-spheres#post1291864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit vs Dimensional Science: Essentially the same, no measurable difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mistaken-ish.<br /> <br /> The most basic difference, that was here from 2nd edition onwards, it's that they use inverted Gauntlet charts. Since Spirit/DimSci dificulty it's very often that of the Gauntlet, this is a relevant difference (and not just thematic). For instance: in a hi-tech lab a Spirit user will have a difficulty 10 to Step Sideways while a Dim-Sci user will have 4.<br /> <br /> This was the only difference until Revised VE book, where it's introduced that DimSci have a greater ease breaching the Gauntlet and treating the Umbra as a place, in exchange of being unable to Awaken stuff and generally worse at relating with spirits in a non-hostile way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Correspondence vs Data: Ups and downs, Data gives you a nearly permanent connection to its targets, but it wont work with say, those that don't use internet/cellphones (any Luddite group) nor extra planetary creatures/locations </div> </div> </div>Yup, also Data it's better at processing loads of information as can be seen in their lvl 3, where they can segment the information they receive.<br /> <br /> VE have a version of Correspondence that cares about distances rather than sympathy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Prime vs Primal Utility: Primal Utility is Prime+, you can do everything that regular old Prime <i>PLUS </i>ventures to generate Quintessence. Is there any downside to this?</span> </div> </div> </div><s>You can't create stuff out of nowhere. No fireballs for you.</s><br /> Nop, I was wrong: You can create stuff out of nowehre, you just can't create stuff out of pure Prime Energy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-25-2019, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T10:15:33-08:00","id":1291871,"title":"","content":"I may be wrong, but my read of the ventures (at least at Primal Utility 4) meant that the ventures did limit the use of Quintessence in certain ways. I recall reading something I'm the write up about not being able to fill up a card at a random node that you hadn't tampered with, and that may thus limit access to natural, unaltered sources. I may be mistaken, however.<br /> <br /> As for data, RAW yes. However, I would argue that someone skilled in Data could still mess with positioning in return, creating proxies and misdirection traces. But that is a personal argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T15:38:54-08:00","id":1291997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291864-regular-spheres-vs-technocratic-spheres?p=1291868#post1291868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mistaken-ish.<br /> <br /> The most basic difference, that was here from 2nd edition onwards, it's that they use inverted Gauntlet charts. Since Spirit/DimSci dificulty it's very often that of the Gauntlet, this is a relevant difference (and not just thematic). For instance: in a hi-tech lab a Spirit user will have a difficulty 10 to Step Sideways while a Dim-Sci user will have 4.<br /> <br /> This was the only difference until Revised VE book, where it's introduced that DimSci have a greater ease breaching the Gauntlet and treating the Umbra as a place, in exchange of being unable to Awaken stuff and generally worse at relating with spirits in a non-hostile way.</div> </div> </div> </div>As of <b>M20</b>, Dimensional Science allows manipulation of the Gauntlet, raising or lowering it. No exorcisms, nor <i>Gilgul</i> it seems.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T15:43:29-08:00","id":1291998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291864-regular-spheres-vs-technocratic-spheres?p=1291871#post1291871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be wrong, but my read of the ventures (at least at Primal Utility 4) meant that the ventures did limit the use of Quintessence in certain ways. I recall reading something I'm the write up about not being able to fill up a card at a random node that you hadn't tampered with, and that may thus limit access to natural, unaltered sources. I may be mistaken, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was about Tass creation, and the first two levels are functionally the same, with extra abilities for Primal Utility (unless I am mistaken about Primal Utility doing the same things as Prime)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 02-25-2019, 08:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T01:00:38-08:00","id":1292090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291864-regular-spheres-vs-technocratic-spheres?p=1291997#post1291997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As of <b>M20</b>, Dimensional Science allows manipulation of the Gauntlet, raising or lowering it. No exorcisms, nor <i>Gilgul</i> it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Important: As of M20, Spirit can only lower the Gauntlet to 4 in normal earthspace. Dimensional Science can actually drop the Gauntlet rating to 0. This has two interesting effects:<br /> 1) VE's are actually able to traverse into the Umbra with level 2 of the Sphere - at the cost of pretty much letting everything else through as well.<br /> and<br /> 2) They are able to cross into the Umbra without Avatar Storm damage, if the Avatar Storm is in play. Only the technician lowering the Gauntlet is affected by the damage from the act.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T05:24:54-07:00","id":1297693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291864-regular-spheres-vs-technocratic-spheres?p=1292090#post1292090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Important: As of M20, Spirit can only lower the Gauntlet to 4 in normal earthspace. Dimensional Science can actually drop the Gauntlet rating to 0. This has two interesting effects:<br /> 1) VE's are actually able to traverse into the Umbra with level 2 of the Sphere - at the cost of pretty much letting everything else through as well.<br /> and<br /> 2) They are able to cross into the Umbra without Avatar Storm damage, if the Avatar Storm is in play. Only the technician lowering the Gauntlet is affected by the damage from the act.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also important, thanks. What is your opinion about Primal Utility (given the observations that have been updated in this thread)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-18-2019, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T14:40:11-07:00","id":1297815,"title":"","content":"Primal Utility doesn't let you create glowing swords of Primal Energy, as far as I can tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T17:09:26-07:00","id":1297831,"title":"","content":"- Primal Ventures are capped at level 5, while Nodes are capped at level 10. With PU you can never access the power of Nodes. Not a huge downside, but already PU isn't just Prime +<br /> <br /> - When you destroy a pattern using Prime 4 you don't get to absorb the energy; so you can dissolve a corpse with Prime 4 to release its Quintessence, but the energy is off limits to you. Same would go for trying to turn an enemy's fireball into Quintessence; you can do the PU 2 + Forces 3 rote sure, but you won't get to absorb any of that Quintessence.<br /> <br /> - Any creation of things like fireballs, money from nowhere etc has to be justified with a very rational or scientific paradigm. To fall within Hypereconomics you're dealing with 3D printers, flamethrowers and the like, so like most Technomancers there's the downside of all this bulky equipment.<br /> <br /> - Ventures are generally a lot better than Nodes in that there is less competition to tap into them, and they're ubiquitous in the modern era. The biggest advantage by far.<br /> <br /> - PU is off limits unless you use a Hypereconomic practice, and honestly that has its downsides. Hypereconomics is one of these practices which is incredibly OP with good backgrounds, abilities and many hours invested into solving problems. But a lot of the trickier moments are where you need to act on the fly, and a slow/careful practice will hamper you there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-16T12:57:36-07:00","id":1341688,"title":"","content":"Sorry to do necromancy, but I was checking some things, and this thread has relevance:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291864-regular-spheres-vs-technocratic-spheres?p=1297831#post1297831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Primal Ventures are capped at level 5, while Nodes are capped at level 10. <b>With PU you can never access the power of Nodes.</b> Not a huge downside, but already PU isn't just Prime +</div> </div> </div> </div>M20, p526<br /> As with Prime 1, the hypereconomist can also invest such<br /> energies and can utilize the Prime Force generated by Ventures<br /> <b>as well as other, more mystical sources of Quintessence</b><br /> <br /> So there is no difficulty accessing Nodes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291864-regular-spheres-vs-technocratic-spheres?p=1297831#post1297831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-<br /> - When you destroy a pattern using Prime 4 you don't get to absorb the energy; so you can dissolve a corpse with Prime 4 to release its Quintessence, but the energy is off limits to you. Same would go for trying to turn an enemy's fireball into Quintessence; you can do the PU 2 + Forces 3 rote sure, but you won't get to absorb any of that Quintessence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Understood, but why is relevant? Both Prime and PU are equally limited on this aspect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291864-regular-spheres-vs-technocratic-spheres?p=1297831#post1297831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Any creation of things like fireballs, money from nowhere etc has to be justified with a very rational or scientific paradigm. To fall within Hypereconomics you're dealing with 3D printers, flamethrowers and the like, so like most Technomancers there's the downside of all this bulky equipment.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the Psionics practice? It fits, semi-scientific, Technocracy-friendly and requires little to none equipment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291864-regular-spheres-vs-technocratic-spheres?p=1297831#post1297831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Ventures are generally a lot better than Nodes in that there is less competition to tap into them, and they're ubiquitous in the modern era. The biggest advantage by far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1291864-regular-spheres-vs-technocratic-spheres?p=1297831#post1297831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- PU is off limits unless you use a Hypereconomic practice, and honestly that has its downsides. Hypereconomics is one of these practices which is incredibly OP with good backgrounds, abilities and many hours invested into solving problems. But a lot of the trickier moments are where you need to act on the fly, and a slow/careful practice will hamper you there.</div> </div> </div> </div>M20, p526<br /> As with all other<br /> Technocratic Sphere Effects, this demands the correct<br /> instruments and training, <b>a</b><b><b>lthough</b> certain practices and<br /> instruments (especially dominion and hypereconomics) simply<br /> give the specialist a hunch about the energies in play.</b><br /> <br /> <u><i>Implying</i></u> that other practices can access Primal Utility; is there any clear statement that PU can <i><b>only </b></i>be used with Hypereconomics?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As far as I see (and please <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a>, correct me if I am wrong) Primal Utility IS Prime+","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 07-17-2022, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-19T14:33:55-07:00","id":1342408,"title":"","content":"Primal Utility isn't rooted in a Practice; it's rooted in a Paradigm (in the M20 sense). I don't have my books handy, so I don't know the name off the top of my head; but it's there. Just like Data is rooted in the Paradigm \u201cEverything is Data\u201d. And I'm pretty sure that Void Correspondence and Dimensional Science likewise have a Paradigm associated with them, though the books don't explicitly spell it out that way; instead, they say that you have to buy into Tychoidean Cosmology to use Dimensional Science. <br /> <br /> As for Primal Utility being Prime+: I'll shave to check to be sure; but I think Primal Utility's drawbacks aren't in things it can't do so much as things it has more trouble doing. I mentioned before the glowing swords of Primal Energy; I'm pretty sure that direct channeling or shaping of Primal Energy is either not possible or requires more dots to attempt. In the Revised Syndicate Convention Book, Primal Utility didn't have much of anything it could do with Tass; M20 changed that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}